# Pinned 2026-10-02 by panel 187's compiler engineer, route (1f): a known
# cost, not an intent; a change in either direction turns this case red.
# A head whose line goes on past it: what goes on is told by one message and
# the rest of the line dropped, by `parse/members_below.hero:87` for a
# `record` or a `variant` and `parse/opening.hero:192` for a function. With
# nothing below, the empty block or the missing body is told instead and the
# junk not at all. Rows 131-16a, 131-16b, 131-53b (the `)` untold) and
# 131-53a (the `)` told only once `->` replaces the `:`). Class (b), a
# mistake told only once another is fixed: `adjacent`.
#
# Moved 2026-10-04 with defect 198's repair (lane b9-recovery): a record's or
# a variant's junk is told over nothing below too, its empty block beside it,
# and a closer one too many past a function's junk is told
# (`parse/brace_habit.drop_told`); it pins that now, one message a mistake.

variant T )  #~ expected_end_of_line empty_variant

record Point )  #~ expected_end_of_line empty_record

function f(): i64 )  #~ expected_end_of_line expected_end_of_line
    return 1

function g(): i64 )  #~ missing_body expected_end_of_line

function main()
    print(1)
